From ab47907a867193f77b8e040f1a2edb18a9a6c731 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Wen <jackwen04@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:21:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] kk: Capture transform feedback from the VS or TES with
 a passthrough GS

Metal has no transform feedback, a GS captures it. When a pipeline
captures it from its VS or TES, that stage is lowered for the hardware
after linking, and a copy of it is compiled as compute, feeding a GS that
passes its output through (poly_nir_passthrough_gs), which the pipeline
describes with the key it'll be built from.

The pipeline draws as before while transform feedback and its queries
are inactive. While either is active, kk_cmd_update_xfb_shaders binds the
pipeline drawing through the passthrough GS instead, built at the first
capture: the GS compiled from its key, and a VS holding the pipeline's
code with the capturing stage as compute. A pipeline has one topology
class, which is all a dynamic topology may change, so it needs one
passthrough GS; adjacency draws through it are unrolled to lists first.

The rasterization VS may emulate the viewport Z transform whatever the
pipeline state, so kk_lower_hw_vs takes that instead of the state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
